WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Let's move on to the second half of the 30 to 2 ratio, giving breaths.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.880
Rescue breaths provide the fresh oxygen that the blood needs to carry to the

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.840
brain. But before we begin, make sure you have

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.760
a barrier device at your disposal. Your instructor should have handed them

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.480
out. It could be a CPR pocket mask or a face shield. We always use these when

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.360
possible to protect both you and the patient.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.879
We'll review the steps now as your instructor demonstrates.

00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:30.559
Step one is to open the airway by performing a head tilt

00:00:30.559 --> 00:00:35.040
chin lift. Without opening the airway, air cannot reach the lungs

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.439
because the tongue often blocks the back of the throat in an unresponsive person.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:44.080
To perform a head tilt chin lift, place one hand on the forehead to tilt the

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.560
head back and use the fingers of your other hand

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.799
to lift the chin upward. Step two is delivering the breaths.

00:00:50.799 --> 00:00:55.520
While keeping the airway open, use your thumb and index finger to pinch the nose

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.119
completely closed. Place your mask or mouth over theirs to

00:00:59.119 --> 00:01:03.520
create a tight seal and give two rescue breaths. Each breath

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.760
should last about one second. The most important thing to watch for

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.440
is visible chest rise. You aren't trying to blow as hard as you

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.239
can. You just want to see that chest move up and down. If you don't see the

00:01:16.239 --> 00:01:20.480
chest rise on the first try, reposition the head and attempt a second

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.440
breath. If it still doesn't rise, don't keep

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.879
trying. Immediately go back to your 30 compressions

00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:30.000
and try the breaths again after that set is done.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.080
Remember, we must never interrupt our compressions for more than 10 seconds to

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.199
give these breaths.

